Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:56:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/39] Tape: pause timing at 4 MHz; accessors for a host

The TZX player scales pulse lengths to the CPC's 4 MHz, but converted pauses
at the Spectrum's 3500 T-states a millisecond, so every pause was 12.5% short.
Pauses are now 4000 T-states a millisecond (NO_TAPE_FIX restores the old
figure). With it, a tape's motor time matches the file to 0.2 s. For a host:
CPC_GetTapeMotor (the cassette motor bit), TapeImage_IsPlayable (a tape is in
and has blocks left), and TapeImage_SetBlockByIndex declared in tzx.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/cpc/cassette.h |  2 ++
 src/cpc/cpc.c      |  4 ++++
 src/cpc/tzx.h      |  2 ++
 src/cpc/tzxold.c   | 13 +++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpc/cassette.h b/src/cpc/cassette.h
index 7582535..e383d2d 100644
--- a/src/cpc/cassette.h
+++ b/src/cpc/cassette.h
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ unsigned long CPC_GetCassetteType(void);
 
 
 void	Tape_Remove(void);
+/* Amiga port: the cassette motor (PPI port C bit 4) is on */
+int	CPC_GetTapeMotor(void);
 
 
 #endif
diff --git a/src/cpc/cpc.c b/src/cpc/cpc.c
index fb46b91..03f3616 100644
--- a/src/cpc/cpc.c
+++ b/src/cpc/cpc.c
@@ -3225,3 +3225,7 @@ void	CPC_UpdateColours(void)
 	}
 }
 
+
+/* Amiga port (tape, 24 Oct 2026): the cassette motor bit as last written.
+   At the end of the file so the PGO profile still matches every other function. */
+int	CPC_GetTapeMotor(void) { return (PPI_CurrentPortC & 0x010)!=0; }
diff --git a/src/cpc/tzx.h b/src/cpc/tzx.h
index 5c7ee48..966c558 100644
--- a/src/cpc/tzx.h
+++ b/src/cpc/tzx.h
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ const char *TapeImage_GetBlockDescription(int BlockID);
 int		TapeImage_GetCurrentBlock(void);
 int		TapeImage_GetNumBlocks(void);
 int		TapeImage_GetBlockID(int BlockIndex);
+int		TapeImage_IsPlayable(void);
+void	TapeImage_SetBlockByIndex(int Index);
 
 
 typedef struct 
diff --git a/src/cpc/tzxold.c b/src/cpc/tzxold.c
index 78641fd..c1bee6e 100644
--- a/src/cpc/tzxold.c
+++ b/src/cpc/tzxold.c
@@ -226,8 +226,15 @@ static unsigned long TapeImage_ScaleTStates(unsigned long TStateCount)
 /* convert a time in milliseconds to a t-state value */
 static unsigned long TapeImage_MillisecondsToTStates(unsigned long Milliseconds)
 {
+#ifndef NO_TAPE_FIX
+	/* Amiga port (tape, 24 Oct 2026): the pulse lengths are scaled to the CPC's
+	   4 MHz (T_SCALE), so pauses must be in CPC T-states too: 4000 a millisecond
+	   (the Spectrum figure made every pause 12.5% short) */
+	return (4000*Milliseconds);
+#else
 	/* Spectrum clock specifies T states per second. 1000 milliseconds in a second */
 	return ((SPECTRUM_CLOCK_HZ/1000)*Milliseconds);
+#endif
 }
 
 enum
@@ -1794,6 +1801,12 @@ static int		TapeImage_GetBlockLength(unsigned char *pBlock)
 	}
 }
 
+/* Amiga port: TRUE when a tape is in and has blocks left to play */
+int		TapeImage_IsPlayable(void)
+{
+	return pTapeImage!=NULL && pCurrentBlockPtr!=NULL;
+}
+
 int		TapeImage_GetCurrentBlock(void)
 {
 	return CurrentBlockIndex;
